// An `else if` chain whose answer is written on a later rung alone. A rung's
// written answer types that rung's case; the chain is the head's case, whose
// head writes none, so where nothing states its type, as at a `run` binding
// it, the chain is not synthesisable (#2089).

/// The answer written on the second rung only: the chain's head answers
/// nothing, so the `run` binding it reads no type off it.
@[ refuses("NotSynthesisable") ]
def answered() -> Integer {
  run n <- if false { pure 0 } else if true -> -F Integer { pure 1 } else { pure 2 };
  pure n
}
